    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.surround\r\n\r\n### Suggestion\r\n\r\nTo define keys outside of `mini.surround`:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- mini_indent.lua\r\n\r\n-- There is no point in overriding `sd` because it would force all keys to be defined in a single place\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"sdi\", function()\r\n  vim.cmd(\"sil norm \" .. string.rep(\"[i\", vim.v.count - 1) .. \"viiy']vaiopgv<\")\r\nend, { desc = \"Unscope\" })\r\n```\r\n\r\nAllow something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- mini_surround.lua\r\n\r\ncustom_surroundings = {\r\n  i = \"\", -- Disable\r\n  i = false, -- Forward keys\r\n  i = {\r\n    -- I don't know which keys are pressed to manually feed them in function\r\n    input = false,\r\n    output = false,\r\n  },\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is needed to avoid ambiguity between `sd` + `i` and `sdi`.\r\n\r\nI feel like the answer is no, but I don't know why yet.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.surround</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Suggestion</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To define keys outside of <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.surround</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"-- mini_indent.lua\n\n-- There is no point in overriding `sd` because it would force all keys to be defined in a single place\nvim.keymap.set(&quot;n&quot;, &quot;sdi&quot;, function()\n  vim.cmd(&quot;sil norm &quot; .. string.rep(&quot;[i&quot;, vim.v.count - 1) .. &quot;viiy']vaiopgv&lt;&quot;)\nend, { desc = &quot;Unscope&quot; })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> mini_indent.lua</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> There is no point in overriding `sd` because it would force all keys to be defined in a single place</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>sdi<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">cmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>sil norm <span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">string.rep</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>[i<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">v</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">count</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">-</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">..</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>viiy']vaiopgv&lt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>Unscope<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Allow something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"-- mini_surround.lua\n\ncustom_surroundings = {\n  i = &quot;&quot;, -- Disable\n  i = false, -- Forward keys\n  i = {\n    -- I don't know which keys are pressed to manually feed them in function\n    input = false,\n    output = false,\n  },\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> mini_surround.lua</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_surroundings</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">i</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Disable</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">i</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>, <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Forward keys</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">i</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> I don't know which keys are pressed to manually feed them in function</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">input</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>,\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">output</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>,\n  },</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is needed to avoid ambiguity between <code class=\"notranslate\">sd</code> + <code class=\"notranslate\">i</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">sdi</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I feel like the answer is no, but I don't know why yet.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.surround\nSuggestion\nTo define keys outside of mini.surround:\n-- mini_indent.lua\n\n-- There is no point in overriding `sd` because it would force all keys to be defined in a single place\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"sdi\", function()\n  vim.cmd(\"sil norm \" .. string.rep(\"[i\", vim.v.count - 1) .. \"viiy']vaiopgv<\")\nend, { desc = \"Unscope\" })\nAllow something like this:\n-- mini_surround.lua\n\ncustom_surroundings = {\n  i = \"\", -- Disable\n  i = false, -- Forward keys\n  i = {\n    -- I don't know which keys are pressed to manually feed them in function\n    input = false,\n    output = false,\n  },\nThis is needed to avoid ambiguity between sd + i and sdi.\nI feel like the answer is no, but I don't know why yet.",
