            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> This is needed to avoid ambiguity between `sd` + `i` and `sdi`.\r\n> \r\n> I feel like the answer is no, but I don't know why yet.\r\n\r\nThe feeling is reasonable. Mostly because intentionally creating conflicting mappings is a bad idea.\r\n\r\nThis is reasonable and possible for `custom_textobjects` in 'mini.ai' because it already takes over a key that is part of built-in textobjects. But 'mini.surround' defines its own keys/actions.\r\n\r\nThe suggestion, I am afraid, is either to not create conflicting mappings or still use the longer one but type fast.",
            "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is needed to avoid ambiguity between <code class=\"notranslate\">sd</code> + <code class=\"notranslate\">i</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">sdi</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I feel like the answer is no, but I don't know why yet.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The feeling is reasonable. Mostly because intentionally creating conflicting mappings is a bad idea.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is reasonable and possible for <code class=\"notranslate\">custom_textobjects</code> in 'mini.ai' because it already takes over a key that is part of built-in textobjects. But 'mini.surround' defines its own keys/actions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The suggestion, I am afraid, is either to not create conflicting mappings or still use the longer one but type fast.</p>",
            "bodyText": "This is needed to avoid ambiguity between sd + i and sdi.\nI feel like the answer is no, but I don't know why yet.\n\nThe feeling is reasonable. Mostly because intentionally creating conflicting mappings is a bad idea.\nThis is reasonable and possible for custom_textobjects in 'mini.ai' because it already takes over a key that is part of built-in textobjects. But 'mini.surround' defines its own keys/actions.\nThe suggestion, I am afraid, is either to not create conflicting mappings or still use the longer one but type fast.",
